European human rights law addresses the issue of unequal treatment based on personal characteristics through various legal frameworks and international treaties, primarily focusing on non-discrimination principles. Key instruments include the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR) and the Council Directive 76/207/EEC on the Implementation of the Principle of Equal Treatment for Men and Women.

